{"title":"2012 CIMC Problems/Part A Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Which of the following is the largest: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/8/2481387c7ae7c22e21843a8ed831291bd16f34b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1^{20}, 2^{14}, 4^{8}, 8^{5}, 16^{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"139\" height=\"20\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can clearly see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/3/fb33abf1d853d58e40d6c2d01be21385d436df84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1^{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"17\" /> would be the lowest because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to any power is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and the other numbers would be a lot greater compared to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Next, using exponent rules, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/e/77ef7fb9e1aba000610d5ddc7d12abb0cbf094b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4^{8} = (2^{2})^{8} = 2^{2 \\times 8} = 2^{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"186\" height=\"21\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/6/cb6973a9804e074c86551c383add40c14419262c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8^{5} = (2^{3})^{5} = 2^{3 \\times 5} = 2^{15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"186\" height=\"21\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/b/d1b47e697065f6ccae444e4d1aa697afdf761a61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16^{3} = (2^{4})^{3} = 2^{4 \\times 3} = 2^{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"195\" height=\"21\" />. Since the numbers now have the same bases, we can look at which number has the highest exponent to see which number is the largest. This would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/f/ebfc79bbd3ccc9d92286e70e51d81a3a9648d5d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{16}$\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c12f9404ac715af84a51c9587d00a29f7d278b31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{4^{8}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"30\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CIMC\" title=\"2012 CIMC\">2012 CIMC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CIMC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2012 CIMC Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CIMC_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2012 CIMC Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</t